<title>UK: Littlewoods adds Index stores, warehouse.</title>
<headline>Littlewoods adds Index stores, warehouse.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The private owners of British high street catalogue retailer Index said on Monday it intended to launch five more stores and had opened a regional distribution centre with the creation of more than 480 jobs.</p>
<p>Index, owned by The Littlewoods Organisation, said in a statement it was spending 3.0 million stg on the stores across Britain and had built and equipped the distribution centre in the Midlands for over 20 million stg.</p>
<p>The new stores will bring the total number of Index stores in the national chain to 140.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
